/* meow-ios — Persian (fa) localization.

   Key set is 1:1 with en.lproj — every key in en.lproj/Localizable.strings
   appears here, in the same order, with a real translation. Strings
   deliberately omitted from en.lproj (QA/OCR harness pins, stable diagnostic
   reason codes, internal chart bindings, log-level Picker .tag() values)
   must NOT be added here either — see en.lproj header for the exclusion list.

   Terminology follows meow-android values-fa/strings.xml: Config → پیکربندی,
   Profile → پروفایل, Proxy → پروکسی, Engine → هسته, Rule → قانون,
   Logs → گزارش‌ها, Latency → تأخیر, Upload / Download → آپلود / دانلود,
   Route Mode → حالت مسیریابی (Rule / Global / Direct → قوانین / سراسری / مستقیم).

   Style:
     - Persian ی (U+06CC) and ک (U+06A9); ZWNJ (U+200C) per standard
       orthography (می‌شود، گروه‌ها); ezafe after ه written as هٔ (U+0654),
       matching values-fa.
     - Technical identifiers and brand names (Shadowsocks, Mihomo, Clash, YAML,
       DNS, TCP, UDP, HTTP/3, QUIC, TUN, TLS, SNI, ECH, DIRECT, no-resolve, …)
       stay in Latin script. Short labels are phrased to start with a Persian
       word where possible so the line keeps a right-to-left base direction.
     - No bidi control characters (unlike values-fa, arguments are not wrapped
       in FSI/PDI); SwiftUI handles RTL layout.
     - Digits written in the source stay Western; runtime numbers follow the
       device locale. Ellipsis is the single character "…" (U+2026). */


